From 0e92ccaea06afafe52c8513761e933f981bb79aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:32:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Diagnostic: sample GLORYS at the wet centre of partial bottom
 cells on the open sides (not for the merge)

nested_ocean_model (NumericalEarth.jl#676) samples the parent at rnode, the centre of the whole cell, which for a
partial bottom cell lies below the model's sea floor. boundary_wet_center_fix.jl samples at the centre of the wet
part instead (on with [boundaries] sample_wet_center = true); config_smoke_test_wet_center.toml is the smoke test
with it. analysis/boundary_bottom_cells.jl lists, for every open side, the partial bottom cells of the boundary row
where GLORYS at the two depths differs most, with the model's value there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
